{
  "id": "find-all-anagrams-in-a-string",
  "questionId": "find-all-anagrams-in-a-string",
  "slug": "find-all-anagrams-in-a-string",
  "title": "Find All Anagrams in a String",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "fixed-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "grind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "this is almost exactly the same question as checking whether one string contains a permutation of another - what's different here?",
    "instead of returning as soon as you find one matching window, what should you do differently?",
    "slide a window the size of p across s, maintaining a running letter-frequency count, updating incrementally as the window moves",
    "whenever the window's frequency count matches p's, record the window's starting index and keep going instead of stopping"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "stopping at the first match instead of collecting all of them",
    "recomputing the frequency count from scratch at each window instead of updating it as you slide",
    "returning the matched substrings instead of their starting indices"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `s` and `p`.\n\n**Find the starting index of every substring of `s` that is an anagram of `p`, and return those indices in increasing order.**\n\nAn anagram uses exactly the same letters with the same counts, in any order.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= s.length <= 3 * 10^4",
      "1 <= p.length <= 3 * 10^4",
      "s and p consist of lowercase English letters only"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "p is longer than s (answer is empty)",
      "overlapping matches right next to each other",
      "s and p share no letters at all"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"cbaebabacd\", p = \"abc\"",
        "output": "[0, 6]",
        "expectedOutput": "[0, 6]",
        "explanation": "\"cba\" at index 0 and \"bac\" at index 6 are both anagrams of \"abc\""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"abab\", p = \"ab\"",
